{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The thigh of Jacob.</b> Out of propriety and modesty, Scripture mentions the place near the organ of generation. And in Mishnaic idiom: 'A woman becomes jealous only of the thigh of her companion' (Megillah 13a). And elsewhere: 'he took the legs' — for they too are near it, as it is written, 'he did not make his legs.'" "<b>Who came out of the thigh of Jacob.</b> He himself was not of the count of the seventy." "<b>Seventy souls.</b> To recount the wonders of HaShem, this verse was written: that with seventy souls our ancestors went down to Egypt. And in two hundred and ten years that they were there, they multiplied to sixty myriads of mighty men, apart from the elderly and the women and the little ones." "<b>And Joseph was in Egypt.</b> Regarding the others it writes 'who came to Egypt,' but this one was not with them — rather he was there before their coming, and he is of the count. Therefore it says <b>and Joseph was in Egypt</b>."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:43.285131090Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}